# WI-16 T1.1 — RED: the integration surface refuses to pass empty

Observed 2026-09-25 at `aec13df`, immediately after `vitest.integration.config.ts`,
the `test:integration` script and the `tsconfig.json` include were added, and
**before** `tests/integration/fixture.test.ts` existed. The output below is that
run, transcribed verbatim.

It is not re-runnable as printed: the command now finds the test file T1.2 added.
Re-running it today shows the T1.2 RED instead — see `t1-guard-absent-fixture.log`.

```
$ npm run test:integration

> software-factory-loop@0.0.0 test:integration
> vitest run --config vitest.integration.config.ts


 RUN  v5.0.0 /home/bitcot/Documents/projects/software-factory-loop

No test files found, exiting with code 1

include: tests/integration/**/*.test.ts
exclude:  **/node_modules/**, **/.git/**

exit=1
```

The point of the observation: `passWithNoTests: false` is what makes this exit 1
rather than 0. An integration command that finds no tests must fail — a check
that cannot fail is not evidence, and a gate that passes on an empty directory
is the vacuous-pass shape this work item exists to remove.

Checked in the same step, unchanged by it:

```
$ npm test          → Test Files 10 passed (10); Tests 287 passed (287); 1.45s
$ npm run typecheck → exit 0
```